<interrogationes unitas="figura">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I make a widget draw itself?
    <responsum symbolum="figura_registrare pingere FiguraFn">Register a
      FiguraFn for the widget's partes and a thema with
      figura_registrare, then call pingere on the logical tree. pingere
      opens one coetus per componens (fines, sectio, translatio, scala,
      provenientia = the componens id), calls the registered figura,
      then walks the children, so a parent always paints UNDER its
      children. The figura draws in the componens' own space: the
      origin is the top-left corner of its fines. figura_registrare
      returns FALSUM for a NIHIL fn or an already registered (partes,
      thema) pair; a componens with no figura still gets its coetus and
      its children are still painted.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what is the thema argument of figura_registrare and pingere, and does it pick the colours?
    <responsum symbolum="pingere figura_color_thematis color_ex_mandato thema_color">It
      is only a key: an i32 that chooses which set of registered
      figurae draws the tree (probatio_figura registers figura_finium
      under thema I next to its thema ZEPHYRUM figura). The figura also
      receives it, but nothing here turns it into colours. A figura
      names colours as ColorMandati, normally through
      figura_color_thematis (genus COLOR_MANDATI_THEMA), and the
      rasterizer resolves them later in color_ex_mandato through
      thema_color, which reads the single process-wide semantic map of
      thema.h.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can a widget inside a mounted pane use figurae registered in the host registry?
    <responsum symbolum="figura_invenire_in_spatio figura_registrum_miscere_in_spatio componens_spatium">No.
      Lookup is strict per spatium: pingere uses the componens'
      effective spatium (the nearest ancestor that sets one, see
      componens_spatium), and figura_invenire_in_spatio only matches
      entries of that exact spatium, with no fallback to the host
      spatium. Merge the pane's own registry into the host with
      figura_registrum_miscere_in_spatio. Entries that already carry a
      spatium (nested panes) keep theirs. The spatium chorda is stored
      as given, not copied, so it must live as long as the registry
      (pass an interned one).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I merge two figure registries that both define the same (partes, thema)?
    <responsum symbolum="figura_registrum_miscere figura_registrum_miscere_in_spatio figura_registrum_vacare">No.
      Merging is all or nothing: if any entry of the source collides
      with an entry already in the target (same partes, thema and
      spatium), the merge returns FALSUM and adds nothing. Collisions
      among entries of the source itself are not checked. To rebuild a
      registry from scratch, figura_registrum_vacare empties it and
      keeps its memory.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why do the figura helpers copy text into the Mandata piscina before drawing it?
    <responsum symbolum="mandata_textus chorda_transcribere figura_textum_audacem figura_globulum_pingere">mandata_textus
      stores the chorda you pass by reference, it does not copy the
      bytes. If the text lives in a temporary buffer, the command list
      points at stale memory by the time it is rasterized. Every text
      helper here (figura_globulum_pingere, figura_segmentum_pingere,
      figura_textum_audacem) first copies the text with
      chorda_transcribere into md-&gt;piscina. Do the same when you call
      mandata_textus yourself.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I draw a standard button, checkbox or segmented control in the house style?
    <responsum symbolum="figura_globulum_pingere figura_sagittam_pingere figura_segmentum_pingere figura_capsam_pingere">Use
      the V1 helpers: figura_globulum_pingere (button),
      figura_sagittam_pingere (arrow button, directio -1 left, +1
      right), figura_segmentum_pingere (one segment, positio
      FIGURA_SEGMENTUM_PRIMUM, _MEDIUM or _ULTIMUM) and
      figura_capsam_pingere(md, x, y, factum) (a IX by IX checkbox at
      x, y, ticked when factum). For the first three, status is a mask
      of FIGURA_ELECTUM (filled with COLOR_SELECTION), FIGURA_UMBRA and
      FIGURA_OBSCURUM (dim text). With FIGURA_UMBRA the body shrinks
      by II pixels (a segment only in height, except _ULTIMUM) and the
      shadow stays inside the given fines, so nothing is painted
      outside the component. Text is centred assuming a 6x8 glyph per
      byte of the chorda.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I paint a pane background with the focus indicator?
    <responsum symbolum="figura_mensam_pingere motus_ramus_focatus FIGURA_EXEMPLAR_FOCI">Call
      figura_mensam_pingere(md, fines, focatum): it fills the fines with
      COLOR_SUPERFICIES and, when focatum is VERUM, lays the
      FIGURA_EXEMPLAR_FOCI pattern in COLOR_BORDER over it (surface
      first, pattern second). It takes a plain b32 so the figura stays
      pure; decide focus with motus_ramus_focatus before
      painting.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
